 # Add Tattler receive cooperative interruption tool
 
-Add a cooperative Tattler receive affordance so an agent can intentionally yield its current turn to check pending messages without showing Operation Aborted.
-
-This is not the sole correctness path; before_agent_start remains the universal drain for any next turn. tattler_receive is a latency/semantics tool for model-initiated interruption.
-
-Acceptance criteria:
-- Tool has tight prompt guidance and is intended to be called alone.
-- Tool renderCall communicates that the agent is checking pending messages / ending the current turn; renderResult is quiet.
-- Tool returns provider-safe content and terminate=true, and sets state for a deferred synthetic receive turn.
-- agent_end scheduling waits until the session is idle before triggering the synthetic turn.
-- Synthetic turn drains through before_agent_start, not a separate delivery path.
-- Tests cover ignored nudge, cooperative receive, and user abort fallback.
-
+Updated synthetic receive design: do not use pi.sendUserMessage to trigger receive because it always renders as a user/Doug message and is semantically misleading. Use pi.sendMessage(batchCustomMessage,{triggerTurn:true}) after idle instead. Source says sendCustomMessage(triggerTurn:true) calls _runAgentPrompt(appMessage), emits/persists the role custom prompt as custom_message, and convertToLlm sends custom content as user-role content to the provider. tattler_receive should set a receive-after-agent-end flag and terminate:true; agent_end idle-defers, then calls shared drainPendingInboxToBatch() and pi.sendMessage(batch,{triggerTurn:true}). before_agent_start remains the user-resume drain path, not the synthetic receive path.
+
